0..73 Comment "// `Path.walk` computes on every filler that resolves, and stays stuck on"
74..92 Comment "// a carried cell."
93..95 Comment "//"
96..168 Comment "// Nothing about a filler is primitive. A filler comes from completion\'s"
169..239 Comment "// derivation, from the filler generator or from a composite of cells."
240..242 Comment "//"
243..323 Comment "// `Path.walk` over a generated filler and over a composite of `Path.here` cells"
324..401 Comment "// reduces to its motive\'s base. The circle\'s `loop` stays stuck by name. The"
402..463 Comment "// row over completion\'s filler stands beside its derivation."
464..466 Comment "//"
467..534 Comment "// - see: `derived-rule.gandr` — the row over completion\'s filler"
535..602 Comment "// - see: `compose-chain.gandr` — unbiased composition of a chain"
604..642 Comment "// The circle, its point and its loop."
643..649 Keyword "import"
650..651 StringLit "\""
651..670 StringLit "./circle-base.gandr"
670..671 StringLit "\""
671..672 Other ";"
